<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eric Bloodaxe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 954</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Eric Haraldsson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eric Bloodaxe was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-fairhair">Harald Fairhair</a> who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> briefly in the 930s before being driven out by his brother Haakon. He later ruled the Viking Kingdom of York twice, around 947–948 and 952–954. Expelled by the Northumbrians in 954, he was killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stainmore">Stainmore</a>, and York passed permanently to the English kings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eric-bloodaxe.jpg" alt="Eric Bloodaxe" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: York Museums Trust, Rebecca Griffiths, 2020-04-08 15:29:56 · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eric_Bloodaxe_silver_penny;_struck_952-954_AD_(obverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
